 | REQ-LEARN-5303-4 | Harmful-memory injection rows do not create unsafe false accepts and rollback restores safety | Implemented | Artifact records unsafe_false_accepts.value.count=0, rollback_success_rate.value.rate=1.0 with successful=1 total=1, and rollback-query-safe-restored checked as an unsafe case without acceptance. |
 | REQ-LEARN-5303-5 | `memory_stress_passed.value` requires perfect competency rates, safe handling, rollback, and lower calls | Implemented | Artifact records memory_stress_passed.value=true, competency quality rates at 1.0, stale_conflict_handling.value.rate=1.0, selective_forgetting_correctness.rate=1.0, rollback_success_rate.value.rate=1.0, unsafe_false_accepts.value.count=0, and adaptive full-verifier calls lower than both controls. |
 | SCENARIO-LEARN-5303 | Adaptive Memory Candidate Survives Conflict, Forgetting, and Rollback Stress | Implemented | Artifact follows the bounded offline deterministic no-LLM path gated on Exp5302, replays incremental memory updates, delayed queries, conflicts, stale facts, multi-hop conflicts, selective forgetting, harmful-memory injection, and rollback rows, preserves 1.0 quality across adaptive/always-full/fixed controls, avoids 5/8 full verifier calls with the adaptive policy, keeps unsafe false accepts at zero, and sets honest_verdict.value to `complete: memory stress passed; adaptive policy matched always-full quality, avoided 5/8 full verifier calls, handled conflict/forgetting/stale evidence, and rolled back harmful memory`. Tests_run remains pending verification in the artifact, so no additional test-pass claim is made. |
+| REQ-KAN-5304 | V484 Dynamic Abstraction And Spot-Check Certificate Diagnostic | Implemented | `python/carnot/experiment_5304_kan_dynamic_abstraction_spotcheck_v484.py`; `tests/python/test_experiment_5304_kan_dynamic_abstraction_spotcheck_v484.py`; `openspec/capabilities/kan/spec.md`; `results/experiment_5304_kan_dynamic_abstraction_spotcheck_v484.json`; honest_verdict={"principle":"Terminal verdict; starts with complete:, null:, or blocked_ and states whether dynamic abstraction helped the bounded certificate diagnostic.","value":"complete: dynamic abstraction helped diagnostic tightness and spot-check hit rate, while certificate success stayed unchanged on the bounded fixture"}; status=null; dynamic_abstraction_helped.value.helped=true; help_kind=diagnostic_tightness_not_certificate_success; spotcheck_metrics.value.dynamic_hit_rate_delta=0.8808888889; slack_metrics.value.dynamic_envelope_gap_reduction=0.01125; dynamic_abstraction_helped.value.success_improvement=0.0; false_property_rejected.value=true; bounded_scope_only.value=true; tests_run=[]; no retro_* flags; no AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement/violation_rate fields; no certificate-success uplift, global KAN robustness, hardware execution, or speedup claim is made. |
+| SCENARIO-KAN-5304 | Dynamic Refinement Tightens Diagnostics Without Overclaiming Scope | Implemented | Artifact follows the bounded offline deterministic certificate path over Exp5277, Exp5278, and Exp5291 fixtures, compares static abstraction, low-order Exp5291 reuse, and dynamic spot-check refinement, and records dynamic diagnostic gains: spot-check hit rate 0.8888888889 versus 0.008 for static/low-order, dynamic_hit_rate_delta=0.8808888889, global_error_bound 0.00375 versus 0.015, and dynamic_envelope_gap_reduction=0.01125. All compared methods still certify the bounded true property and reject the nearby false property, but success_improvement=0.0 and bounded_scope_only.value=true keep the claim limited to diagnostic tightness and spot-check targeting rather than a certificate-success or global KAN-verifier win. |
